  "announcementAllGoodBody": "No major academic risks detected right now.",
  "faqStartedQ1": "How do I log in?",
  "faqStartedA1": "Tap \"Sign in\" on the welcome screen and enter the email or username your school administrator gave you, plus your temporary password. You'll be asked to set a new password the first time.",
  "faqStartedQ2": "I don't have a login yet.",
  "faqStartedA2": "Your school administrator creates accounts. Ask them to add you — they'll give you a username or email and a temporary password.",
  "faqStartedQ3": "Can I use the app in my language?",
  "faqStartedA3": "Yes — ClassMate supports English, Arabic, Hebrew, French and Russian. Open Settings → Language to switch.",
  "faqStartedQ4": "How do I switch between dark and light mode?",
  "faqStartedA4": "Open Settings → Appearance → Theme. Pick \"System default\" to follow your device's light or dark mode, or choose one of 20 themes — you can also make your own.",
  "faqAccountQ1": "I forgot my password.",
  "faqAccountA1": "Tap \"Forgot password?\" on the login screen. We'll send a reset link by email or by text message (SMS), in your language. If neither your email nor your phone is verified yet, ask your school administrator to set a new temporary password.",
  "faqAccountQ2": "How do I change my password?",
  "faqAccountA2": "Open Profile from the drawer, scroll to Security, and tap the password row. You'll need your current password to set a new one.",
  "faqAccountQ3": "How do I change my email or phone number?",
  "faqAccountA3": "Open Profile, tap the field you want to change, and follow the verification prompts. A code is sent to your CURRENT email/phone first to confirm it's really you, then you can set the new value.",
  "faqAccountQ4": "My school administrator can change my password — how does that work?",
  "faqAccountA4": "When an administrator resets your password, you'll get an email and SMS with a one-tap link to set your own password. The admin never sees what you choose.",
  "faqStudentsQ1": "Where do I see my schedule?",
  "faqStudentsA1": "Schedule is the first tab at the bottom of the screen. You'll see this week's periods, who teaches each one, and any changes the admin has posted.",
  "faqStudentsQ2": "How do I join a classroom?",
  "faqStudentsA2": "A teacher will add you directly, or share a join code. To use a join code, open the Classrooms tab, tap Join Classroom and type the code.",
  "faqStudentsQ3": "How do attendance and grades work?",
  "faqStudentsA3": "Teachers mark attendance during the lesson. Open Attendance or Grades from the drawer to see your records. Parents linked to your account see the same data.",
  "faqStudentsQ4": "What is NOVA?",
  "faqStudentsA4": "NOVA is your AI study buddy — ask it to explain a concept, generate a quiz, or walk through a problem step by step. Open the NOVA tab to start a chat.",
  "faqTeachersQ1": "How do I create a classroom?",
  "faqTeachersA1": "Open Classrooms from the drawer and tap the + button. Give it a name and subject; students can be added by hand or via a join code.",
  "faqTeachersQ2": "How do I mark attendance?",
  "faqTeachersA2": "Open Attendance from School Tools, pick the date and period, set each student's status, then tap Save.",
  "faqTeachersQ3": "How do I assign homework?",
  "faqTeachersA3": "Open Assignments, tap +, fill in the title/due date/attachments, and pick a target (whole school, specific cohorts, or named students). Students see it right away in their Assignments.",
  "faqTeachersQ4": "Can I issue a certificate?",
  "faqTeachersA4": "Homeroom teachers can — open Certificates from School Tools, pick the class and the student, then create the certificate. You can also build one PDF for the whole class. The student sees it in their own Certificates.",
  "faqAdminsQ1": "Where do I start setting up a school?",
  "faqAdminsA1": "Open the Admin Dashboard. The School Setup widget at the top shows a 7-step checklist (logo, name, subjects, bell schedule, cohorts, students, teachers). Each step deep-links to where you complete it.",
  "faqAdminsQ2": "How do cohorts work?",
  "faqAdminsA2": "A cohort is a group of students that share a schedule. Open Cohorts from School Tools to create them and add students. A single cohort can span multiple grades.",
  "faqAdminsQ3": "Can a cohort cover more than one grade?",
  "faqAdminsA3": "Yes — when creating a cohort, select multiple grades. The cohort then appears in any of those grades' filters and views, and announcements/templates targeted at any of those grades reach it.",
  "faqAdminsQ4": "How do I build the weekly schedule?",
  "faqAdminsA4": "Open Schedule from the drawer. Tap any cell to add a period — pick the day/period, teacher, subject, and audience (cohort/student/grade). Bell-schedule times come from School Settings.",
  "faqAdminsQ5": "How do I bulk-export students?",
  "faqAdminsA5": "Open Export Data. Choose whether to select by student or by cohort, pick the rows, and tap Export. If you include passwords, each exported student gets a new temporary password (the old one stops working) — handy for printing login cards.",
  "faqAdminsQ6": "A user asked me to reset their password. What do I do?",
  "faqAdminsA6": "Open Users, tap the person and set a new password — they also get an email or text with a link to choose their own. If their email or phone is verified, they can reset it themselves with \"Forgot password?\".",
  "faqParentsQ1": "How do I link my account to my child?",
  "faqParentsA1": "Your child's school administrator links your account to your child from their admin app. Once linked, your child appears on your Home screen.",
  "faqParentsQ2": "What can I see about my child?",
  "faqParentsA2": "Attendance, grades, announcements, and homework — exactly what your child sees plus the trends across time. You won't see private chats or NOVA sessions.",
  "faqPrivacyQ1": "Who can see my data?",
  "faqPrivacyA1": "Only people in your school. Teachers see their classrooms' data, admins see school-wide data, parents see their linked children. We never sell data to advertisers.",
  "faqPrivacyQ2": "How do I delete my account?",
  "faqPrivacyA2": "Ask your school administrator to delete it from their admin app, which wipes your profile, schedule, and chats. You can also email support@classmateapp.org from your account's email address and we'll delete it within 30 days.",
